# standard.clock — EAV-native clock binding (§27 planned; §30.5.3 authority model).
#
# Parity with semsc's `std/time` surface, the EAV-clean way: time is authority,
# so a wall-clock read is a capability-mediated effect (injected for determinism,
# §30.5.3; captured under `mode capturedOutputReplay`, §30.1.1). `nowMillis` is a
# `body runtimeBinding` read over the in-process runtime; the unit conversions are
# ordinary pure step-body operations (no effect, no capability) — they compute
# values and so are deterministic and need no authority.

standardClock is module
standardClock path standard.clock
standardClock purpose "Capability-gated wall-clock reads plus pure time-unit conversions"
standardClock invariant "Reading the clock is a capability-mediated effect; conversions are pure"

wallClock is capability
wallClock grants read clock.wall
wallClock purpose "Authority to read the wall clock (inject a fixed clock for deterministic tests)"

nowMillis is operation
nowMillis out Int64
nowMillis effect read clock.wall
nowMillis uses wallClock
nowMillis body runtimeBinding eav_http_now_millis
nowMillis purpose "Current wall-clock time in milliseconds since the Unix epoch (capability-gated)"

secondsToMinutes is operation
secondsToMinutes in seconds Int64
secondsToMinutes out Int64
secondsToMinutes async no
secondsToMinutes purpose "Whole minutes contained in a second count (pure)"
secondsToMinutes let secondsPerMinute immutable Int64 60
secondsToMinutes do divideToMinutes
secondsToMinutes return minutesValue

divideToMinutes is call
divideToMinutes in secondsToMinutes
divideToMinutes invokes math.divideInt64
divideToMinutes arg left Int64 seconds
divideToMinutes arg right Int64 secondsPerMinute
divideToMinutes out minutesValue Int64

minutesToSeconds is operation
minutesToSeconds in minutes Int64
minutesToSeconds out Int64
minutesToSeconds async no
minutesToSeconds purpose "Seconds in a minute count (pure)"
minutesToSeconds let secondsPerMinute immutable Int64 60
minutesToSeconds do multiplyToSeconds
minutesToSeconds return secondsValue

multiplyToSeconds is call
multiplyToSeconds in minutesToSeconds
multiplyToSeconds invokes math.multiplyInt64
multiplyToSeconds arg left Int64 minutes
multiplyToSeconds arg right Int64 secondsPerMinute
multiplyToSeconds out secondsValue Int64
